{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997973-what-if-you-use-enhancements-on-other-splats","id":997973,"title":"What if you use enhancements on other splats?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-03T17:29:42-07:00","id":997973,"title":"What if you use enhancements on other splats?","content":"So what if you embrace one of the 'Victors' or the first change happens to a recepient of SuperKidneyTM. A walking machine-man of paradox gets possessed while hospitalized or your xenomodded freak gets reclaimed by the deviants it borrowed from. I can't imagine many storytellers saying yes to a character with biomods or whatnot, and I'm pretty sure they'll just cause garou battlescars done wrong and Vampires lacking fleshcraft will probably just heal it when they sleep (good thing vampires sleep so deeply, I imagine they'd pop out pretty painfully) <br /> <br /> But... what if? Can it even be done in fluff (if not balanced mechanics)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T17:59:05-07:00","id":997987,"title":"","content":"Depends on the other splat. Vampires have obvious issues with their rejection. But IIRC the Tremere have a solution for that. Not that it would generally work within the technocracy because they'd be forced to give up blood magic the moment they got processed.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, a Garou would just gain the benefits of the enhancements. Essentially an enhancement is just an artifact/device that's been made to bind directly to and integrate itself with a living pattern. Whether that's the ruby slippers or a robotic arm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 11-03-2016, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T18:16:42-07:00","id":997993,"title":"","content":"Who knows? Maybe the conflicting static and dynamic magic within them would cause unintended effects, especially if you consider paradox. Being gene modded to trait 6s only to discover you're also a werewolf may be awesome at first, until you also start growing a vestigial third arm from your back. Not to mention an alien and powerful breed of spirit(the paradox ones) is now gunning for your head on a plate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T02:44:59-07:00","id":998153,"title":"","content":"All I know is that cybernetics don't work on vamps (<i>The Red Sign 2003, p 47</i>). Progenitors would be the most successful at doing something, in a similar fashion to Vicissitude and blood magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T04:17:40-07:00","id":998167,"title":"","content":"But what if you embraced em while they had all that stuff installed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T06:32:08-07:00","id":998202,"title":"","content":"Iterators, HIT marks and machine freaks in general cannot be embraced, nor ghouled. Their blood is toxic and causes aggravated damage to any vampire trying to drink it.<br /> <br /> Assuming that they can be embraced, the enhancements will simply cease to function, leaving a hole or a scar in its stead or just junk.<br /> <br /> Whether the injuries and amputated limbs could be healed post embrace are <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/929092-appearance-at-embrace-prosthetics\">debatable</a>...but who cares, I doubt the embrace would work anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 11-04-2016, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:10:49-07:00","id":998257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997973-what-if-you-use-enhancements-on-other-splats?p=998202#post998202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iterators, HIT marks and machine freaks in general cannot be embraced, nor ghouled. Their blood is toxic and causes aggravated damage to any vampire trying to drink it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...a vampire doesn't need to <i>drink</i> the blood of someone they're embracing. The victim just needs to be drained, which could easily be done by slitting their throat or wrists and letting them bleed out. It's just that most times, vampires drink the blood as a matter of course. If they realize the blood is toxic, they can proceed with the Embrace if they really want to.<br /> <br /> That said, it's probably not possible to Embrace a HIT Mark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:54:01-07:00","id":998351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/997973-what-if-you-use-enhancements-on-other-splats?p=998153#post998153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I know is that cybernetics don't work on vamps (<i>The Red Sign 2003, p 47</i>). Progenitors would be the most successful at doing something, in a similar fashion to Vicissitude and blood magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weird. I recall that according to The World of Future Darkness, there's a ritual known by Mages and the Tremere that allows installing (workable) cybernetics into a vampire even after Embrace. IIRC there was even a way to make cybernetic celerity stack with vampiric Celerity (and presumably with Time magick).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:20:15-07:00","id":998368,"title":"","content":"Ok was going to quote a few people but since it would be multiple topics and I suck at doing that I figured just type away.<br /> <br /> Garou with Cybernetics, don't the Glass Walkers already have rules for that? Should be a big deal just to use some of the stuff from Mage just make it cost Gnosis or something to off set the advantage. Ghouls I don't think could use it but they could possibly use the stuff from Demon Hunter X which is very close to the awakened stuff.<br /> <br /> Hit Marks are machines so they can't be embraced, just an organic coating over a metal exoskeleton. You know a Terminator which what they were inspired from, and yes sometimes they even look like Arnold. <br /> <br /> I do think Vicky_molokh is correct I do remember the Future World of Darkness just don't have all my old WW Magazines to check it out. But now that you mention it I do think you are right, and they have stats for different cybernetics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}